cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "sfu-library-thinclient (Duck Library): local-first hybrid academic search over 150M documents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: Gordon
repository-code: "https://github.com/Spicy-Sashimizy/sfu-library-thinclient"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
version: "2026-10-10"
abstract: >-
  Research testbed for a no-cluster academic search stack: tantivy BM25F,
  SPLADE served by SEISMIC from immutable mmap shards, optional dense leg,
  RRF fusion and cross-encoder rerank over a 150-million-document OpenAlex
  corpus, exposed as MCP tools and a web GUI, with every design decision and
  measurement recorded in the repository's docs tree.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - learned sparse retrieval
  - SPLADE
  - SEISMIC
  - BM25F
  - hybrid search
  - Model Context Protocol
